{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Prince of Antioch and Count of Tripoli he was the son of Bertrand I Count of Tripoli and the brother of Bohemond I Prince of Antioch he was born around 1111 and died 1152\n\n* **Early Life and Reign**\nRaymond III was born in 1111 to Bertrand I Count of Tripoli and his wife Garsinde he received a military education and was trained in the art of war from an early age he became the Count of Tripoli in 1135 after the death of his father he was crowned King of Jerusalem in 1152\n\n* **Military Campaigns**\nRaymond III was a skilled military leader and participated in many campaigns during his reign he led a campaign against the Fatimid Caliphate in 1148 and was defeated at the Battle of Inab he also participated in the Second Crusade and was a key leader in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177\n\n* **Family and Succession**\nRaymond III was married to Eschiva of Alpilles daughter of William II Count of Alpilles he had no children he was succeeded by his brother Bohemond II Prince of Antioch who went on to have a long and successful reign however Raymond III's death marked the beginning of a period of instability in the County of Tripoli\n\nRaymond III was a member of the House of Hauteville and was a cousin of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem he was a member of the royal family and played an important role in the politics of the kingdom of Jerusalem", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0011805477552115917}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.00011586471373448148}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.19920571148395538}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.802703940891661e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002942844294011593}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.067568756407127e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00881943665444851}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.36243766546249